"""Level Factory 0.227.0: a building's slot that holds what the merge cannot carry stays whole (the factory's install
test 11, certifying factory 1.41.0).

The buildings' merge (0.223.0) copies static bodies out and meshes into the merged meshes and removes each slot it took
apart, so it removed every enterable building's `Ladders` (Deli Counter's Area3D climb volumes) and `Markers` (the
grouped spawns and objectives a game finds by group). Install test 11's walk: "no ladder_area3d in scene". Counted on
two levels' packages before the rule was chosen: the factory's `docs/findings/merge_ladders_227/`.

What it changes (anchored; each file pinned by hash; nothing written on a miss):
  * assets/godot/merge_buildings.gd -- `_cannot_carry` and `_held`: outside a StaticBody3D, a node that is neither a
    MeshInstance3D nor a bare Node3D, or any node in a group of its own or with metadata, keeps its slot whole,
    decided before any collider is copied out; the report's `kept_carrying` names each slot so kept.
  * packages/exporting/merge_buildings.py -- `check` refuses a row without the list; the docstring says why.
  * packages/exporting/export.py -- the export's merge line counts the slots kept whole.
  * tests/unit/test_merge_buildings.py -- the rule held to the source; two refusals; fail on 0.226.2.
  * tests/unit/test_merge_buildings_godot.py (new) -- the Godot half run on a small building; three of its four
    tests fail on 0.226.2.
  * VERSION 0.226.2 -> 0.227.0, CHANGELOG.

Generated by `patches/lf_merge_carries/gen_lf_merge_carries.py` from a proven clone; its dry runs, the prove run and
the suite are beside it.

    python patches/patch_lf_merge_carries.py
"""
